  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday) \nIssued at 1230 PM MDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nAfter PWATs bottom out over northwest areas around 0.50-0.75\" on\nWednesday, they will rebound through the end of the week as a \nsurge of monsoon moisture works its way northward over AZ and \nwestern NM. There will be a chance of locally heavy rainfall \nFriday and Saturday afternoon and evening over western areas, and \nprobably also over the Ruidoso area scars, as PWATs climb around \n1.10-1.30\" across the forecast area. Models vary on how well the \nmonsoon moisture will linger over western areas on Sunday, with \nsome suggesting an ENE to WSW ridge axis over southern NM will \nshift the moisture plume westward over AZ. After continued warming\nThursday, the increased monsoon moisture will cause high \ntemperatures to trend downward at the end of the week.",
